SXAC - Simple X Auto Clicker
----------------------------

SXAC is a simple X Auto Clicker. It is written in C and uses the XTest extension to simulate mouse clicks.


Requirements
------------

libx11 and libxtst are required to build sxac, with their header packages.
XTest has to be enabled in the running X server, which it is by default.


Installation
------------

Build it, where the second line needs root:

$ make
# make install

Or take the prebuilt binary, which is x86-64 and unsigned, so build from source
where that matters:

$ wget https://github.com/h3nc4/sxac/releases/latest/download/sxac
# install -Dm755 sxac /usr/local/bin/sxac


Usage
-----

Run the program with default settings:

$ sxac

This will start the auto clicker with the following default settings:

- Click interval: 100 ms
- Click button: 1 (left mouse button)


To specify a different button, use the -b option followed by the button number:

$ sxac -b 2

The button numbers are:

1   left mouse button
2   middle mouse button
3   right mouse button


To specify a different click interval, use the -d option followed by the interval in milliseconds:

$ sxac -d 200


To display usage information:

$ sxac -h


Stopping it
-----------

sxac clicks wherever the pointer happens to be, so a short interval can make the
desktop hard to use while it runs. Ctrl+C stops it while it holds the foreground
of a terminal. Started in the background, it takes a signal from elsewhere:

$ pkill sxac

Settle on one of those two before starting it with a small -d.


